    "invocation_id": "e-44352cff-8985-4363-9807-22971c1c4506",
    "kind": "agent_answer",
    "from": "repair_agent",
    "text": "The issue \"proxy isatty\" in `rich` suggests that when a file is wrapped by `FileProxy` (e.g., `sys.stdout`), the proxy's behavior might interfere with standard I/O checks, particularly those related to TTY status.\n\nThe `FileProxy.write` method manually constructs output lines and prints them using `self.__console.print(output)`. If `output` already contains newlines (which it does, as it is joined by `\"\\n\"`), calling `console.print(output)` without specifying `end=\"\"` will cause `console.print` to append an extra newline, potentially altering the stream's behavior in a way that affects TTY detection or line-by-line processing.\n\nI have applied a fix by adding `end=\"\"` to `console.print(output)` in `rich/file_proxy.py`.\n\nI will now submit the patch."
  },
